  ;; ---- corpus source datasets (ADR-2608041800) ---------------------------
  ;; Only the index/ layer of these is consumed. raw/ is git-annex content
  ;; living in Backblaze B2 and is NOT fetched by this repository or by its
  ;; CI: a projection must be rebuildable without downloading 3.43 GB of
  ;; statutory text.
  ;;
  ;; :source/ci-checkout false on all four -- and as of 2026-08-05 that is a
  ;; DESIGN STATEMENT, not the gap it used to be. CI is the murakumo fleet
  ;; (scripts/fleet-ci/ in com-junkawasaki/root), and its gate
  ;; legislation-corpus-check verifies the COMMITTED projection by sha256
  ;; instead of checking these sources out. That catches a hand-edited shard,
  ;; which the GitHub Actions design could not: Actions only ever read values
  ;; that were already committed, so nothing regenerated the files and
  ;; `git diff --exit-code -- data` stayed silent.
  ;;
  ;; What is still not done, stated plainly: nobody RE-DERIVES data/corpus/**
  ;; from these locked revisions in CI. Doing that needs their index/ trees on
  ;; a fleet node. The sha256 check makes tampering detectable; it does not
  ;; make the derivation reproducible.
